<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n49561" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Tyăna</span></b> ,
		ōrum, n., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Τύανα</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a city in Cappadocia</i>, <i>the
				birthplace of the philosopher Apollonius</i>, now <i>Kiz Hissar</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 6, 3, 3,
				§ 8</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Amm. 23, 6,
			19</span></i>.—Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Tyă-nēĭus</span></b> ,
				a, um, adj., <i>of</i>
			or <i>belonging to Tyana</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">incola,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. M.
					8, 719</span></i>
			.—Collat. form <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Tyănaeus</span></b> , a, um
			(late Lat.), <i><span class="en">Amm. 21, 14, 5</span></i>.</div>
